## What is a Card? Code → Output {.smaller}

Every code chunk output is automatically wrapped in a card. The `#| title:` option sets the card header.

::: {.panel-tabset}

### Code

````{.markdown filename="card.qmd"}
```{{r}}
#| title: "Beneficiaries by team"
#| fig-height: 4
#| expandable: true
ggplot(df, aes(x = team, y = reach, fill = team)) +
  geom_col(show.legend = FALSE) +
  theme_c4ed()
```
````

### Live preview

```{r}
#| label: card-preview
#| fig-align: center
#| echo: false
library(ggplot2)
df_demo <- data.frame(
  team  = LETTERS[1:5],
  reach = c(412, 538, 297, 614, 480)
)
ggplot(df_demo, aes(team, reach, fill = team)) +
  geom_col(show.legend = FALSE) +
  scale_fill_manual(values = c("#047B77","#1A9490","#65BAB5",
                               "#9FD3D0","#CDEAE8")) +
  labs(title = "Beneficiaries by team",
       x = NULL, y = "Reach") +
  theme_minimal(base_size = 14)
```

### Manual card

```markdown
::: {.card title="Key finding"}
Write any **markdown** here.

- Bullet one
- Bullet two
:::
```

Use a manual `.card` div for **text-only** cards (key findings, notes).

:::

::: {.callout-tip}
`#| expandable: true` adds a fullscreen button to any card.
:::

